<title>MEXICO: Mexico 1996-1997 sugar harvest update to April 19.</title>
<headline>Mexico 1996-1997 sugar harvest update to April 19.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Agroindustry Sugar Committee weekly harvest update for the 1996-1997 (Nov/June) sugar crop to April 19 (sugar, in tonnes) --</p>
<p>Activity in week April 13-April 19</p>
<p>    Harvest	Cane milled	Sugar Output    Yield</p>
<p>     96-97     1,404,901 tns	153,522 tns    10.93 pct</p>
<p>     95-96     1,830,091 tns	214,058 tns    11.70 pct</p>
<p>     94-95     1,577,122 tns	165,161 tns    10.47 pct</p>
<p>Total activity to April 19</p>
<p>    Harvest	Cane milled	Sugar Output    Yield</p>
<p>     96-97    32,025,843 tns    3,469,606 tns    10.83 pct</p>
<p>     95-96    32,046,419 tns    3,463,118 tns    10.81 pct</p>
<p>     94-95    30,316,508 tns    3,229,254 tns    10.65 pct</p>
<p>The committee reported that during the week 59 of the country's active 61 mills were in operation compared to 60 in the 1995-1996 harvest and 58 in the 1994-1995 harvest.</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 728 9530))</p>
</text>
